=== 15888623  https://help.alphacapitalgroup.uk/en/articles/15888623-what-is-the-max-risk-rule-and-how-does-it-work
  +all trading costs, including commissions, swaps and slippage, count toward the threshold.
  +we recommend leaving a buffer below the threshold, as these costs can take a loss beyond the level you planned.
  +this applies to each further trade opened within 10 minutes of the previous trade closing, so a sequence of trades can form a single continuous chain.
  +the chain ends once more than 10 minutes pass between one trade closing and the next trade opening.
  +trades in the opposite direction on the same asset form a separate chain and do not interrupt this one.
  +example:
  +you have a $100,000 alpha pro qualified analyst account and close an xau/usd buy with a $1,000 loss.
  +you open another xau/usd buy 5 minutes later and close it with a $500 loss, then open a third xau/usd buy 7 minutes later.
  +the three trades form one chain, and the max risk rule is breached once the third trade reaches $500 in open drawdown, as the combined loss reaches $2,000 (2%).
  +had the third trade been opened 12 minutes after the second one closed, it would start a new chain, and only its own loss would count toward the threshold.

=== 16003693  https://help.alphacapitalgroup.uk/en/articles/16003693-alpha-direct
